WEBVTT

00:01:01.854 --> 00:01:04.773
Coming, coming.

00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:07.442
Hey. Everything all right, Toriko?

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:08.902
Huh? What?

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.904
Japanese barbeque? Now?

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.614
You want to celebrate?

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:14.408
I guess.

00:01:14.408 --> 00:01:16.451
Okay, Ikebukuro. Got it.

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:20.747
It's not just us? Did you invite Kozakura?

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:24.293
What? Akari, too? Why'd you invite her?

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:43.437
<i>School never taught me what friends are</i>

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:48.817
<i>People are such difficult creatures</i>

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:53.238
<i>This world where you never</i>
<i>know what's said behind your back</i>

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:58.785
<i>Looks a little ugly to me</i>

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:03.665
<i>Compassion and ego sway on the scales</i>

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:08.212
<i>They've swayed ever since I met you</i>

00:02:08.212 --> 00:02:11.131
<i>Your trespassing did a number on me</i>

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:15.427
<i>It's not like anyone would do</i>

00:02:15.427 --> 00:02:15.511
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:15.511 --> 00:02:16.678
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:20.933
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:25.270
<i>Like a fish out of water</i>

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.564
<i>Delicacy and literacy</i>

00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:30.150
<i>Might not be necessary</i>

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.362
<i>I just want to be wanted</i>

00:02:33.362 --> 00:02:35.739
<i>Selfish little me</i>

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:39.910
<i>The scales have tipped</i>

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.162
<i>As friends</i>

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:48.168
<i>Let's meet in a secret place</i>

00:03:03.058 --> 00:03:06.353
Sorry I'm late. Just you so far?

00:03:06.353 --> 00:03:10.148
No, Akari went in to see
if any tables were open.

00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:12.025
We don't have a reservation?

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:15.320
We'll be fine. It's still early.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.489
Talk about a lack of planning.

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:19.366
What about Kozakura?

00:03:19.366 --> 00:03:20.868
She said she's almost here.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.120
Oh, okay.

00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:32.462
What?

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:36.550
Oh, no, I was just wondering.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:40.345
When did you exchange numbers with Akari?

00:03:40.345 --> 00:03:41.346
Huh?

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:44.975
It was Akari's idea to have
Japanese barbeque today, isn't it?

00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:49.438
Oh, Akari asked for my number
right before I left the other day.

00:03:49.438 --> 00:03:50.898
And you told her?

00:03:50.898 --> 00:03:51.940
I shouldn't have?

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:56.778
No, that's not what I meant.

00:03:56.778 --> 00:04:00.949
She could've asked me.
Instead, she went right to you.

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:04.870
She said she tried calling you
but never got through.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.706
Yeah, I tend not to answer.

00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:10.542
Well, there you go.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.755
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:04:14.755 --> 00:04:17.799
If Kozakura's coming, should we
talk to her about you know what?

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:19.551
Hm?

00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:23.222
On second thought, Akari's here, so...

00:04:23.222 --> 00:04:25.390
Talk to her about what?

00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:31.104
About Kisaragi Station.

00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:41.281
You want to go rescue those American soldiers.

00:04:44.076 --> 00:04:46.495
Yeah.

00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:51.375
It's been bothering me
how we left them behind like that.

00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:53.627
But why bring it up now?

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:59.424
You said we couldn't help them
because there's no way to get back there.

00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:03.470
I thought about it,
and there just might be a way.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:04.763
Really?

00:05:04.763 --> 00:05:10.686
You still have that battered old hat?
You know, Lady Hasshaku's?

00:05:12.604 --> 00:05:14.064
It's Akari.

00:05:14.064 --> 00:05:16.275
Akari? Any tables?

00:05:16.275 --> 00:05:19.862
What? It's not there?
As in, it went out of business?

00:05:19.862 --> 00:05:22.865
That's not what you meant?

00:05:22.865 --> 00:05:25.158
Huh? You can't find the restaurant?

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:26.535
Something happen?

00:05:26.535 --> 00:05:27.661
That's strange.

00:05:27.661 --> 00:05:29.997
I know. I can't find it.

00:05:29.997 --> 00:05:30.581
"Akari"
I know. I can't find it.

00:05:30.581 --> 00:05:31.874
"Akari"
Akari, what's the problem?

00:05:31.874 --> 00:05:34.585
"Akari"
Oh, Sorawo! I'm so sorry about this.

00:05:34.585 --> 00:05:37.504
"Akari"
I got off on this weird floor, and now I'm lost.

00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:37.754
I got off on this weird floor, and now I'm lost.

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:40.465
What? How could you get
lost in a building like that?

00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:44.636
Sorry, but it was like someone
was messing with the elevator.

00:05:44.636 --> 00:05:46.847
It kept stopping on different floors.

00:05:46.847 --> 00:05:47.556
Huh?

00:05:47.556 --> 00:05:50.225
I thought I was finally there,
but I ended up on the roof.

00:05:50.225 --> 00:05:51.727
It's really weird, too.

00:05:51.727 --> 00:05:56.064
There's a bright red sunset,
but isn't it dark already?

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:58.692
I thought it was strange,
so I tried to go back down,

00:05:58.692 --> 00:06:00.944
but I just couldn't get to the first floor.

00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:07.075
It stopped at different floors,
and you ended up on the roof?

00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:09.786
Toriko, how many floors are there?

00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:11.205
Ten.

00:06:11.205 --> 00:06:12.998
Akari, what floor are you on?

00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:17.878
I'm on the fifth floor, I think,
but the display's weird.

00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:20.255
Stay right there! We'll come get you.

00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:21.840
Hm? What was that?

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.760
Oh, okay. I'll try to find
the stairs or something.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.261
What? No, wait!

00:06:26.261 --> 00:06:29.932
Huh? Is that you guys over there?
Are you waving at me?

00:06:29.932 --> 00:06:33.477
I didn't know you were so close by.

00:06:33.477 --> 00:06:35.729
What are you talking about? It's not us.

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:38.815
All right, already! I'm coming!

00:06:38.815 --> 00:06:39.691
"Akari"
All right, already! I'm coming!

00:06:39.691 --> 00:06:40.067
"Akari"

00:06:44.071 --> 00:06:46.782
Sorawo, do you think...?

00:06:46.782 --> 00:06:50.285
Yeah, probably.

00:06:50.285 --> 00:06:52.788
It's a way to the Otherside.

00:06:53.789 --> 00:06:57.584
But she got off before she got there.

00:06:58.627 --> 00:07:01.421
To get to the Otherside,

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:05.384
you press the elevator
buttons in a certain order.

00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:08.804
That's how the urban legend says you get there.

00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:13.225
The method we used to get to the
Otherside through the Jinbo-cho gate

00:07:13.225 --> 00:07:16.395
was based on that.

00:07:16.395 --> 00:07:22.442
But I never thought the same
method could be used elsewhere.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:25.112
After all, urban legends are just legends.

00:07:25.112 --> 00:07:30.534
I assumed there were only a few
places connected to the Otherside.

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:34.621
Actually, I really believe that.

00:07:34.621 --> 00:07:37.791
If there were too many ways in,
it would be too easy.

00:07:37.791 --> 00:07:41.545
Or should I say, too dangerous?

00:07:41.545 --> 00:07:47.843
The original story specifies an elevator
in a building that's ten stories or more.

00:07:47.843 --> 00:07:53.223
But there are countless buildings
with that many floors.

00:07:53.223 --> 00:07:57.686
So this building's a gate,
and you can use the same method?

00:07:57.686 --> 00:08:00.564
And Akari just happened to get lost in there?

00:08:00.564 --> 00:08:02.149
Could it be a coincidence?

00:08:02.149 --> 00:08:04.776
No way.

00:08:04.776 --> 00:08:07.779
It's like she was lured in. I don't like this.

00:08:07.779 --> 00:08:12.075
Still, we have to do something,
or else Akari will...

00:08:12.075 --> 00:08:13.452
Yeah.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:20.542
She's probably in the In-Between,
the region between worlds.

00:08:20.542 --> 00:08:23.670
We better go help her before it's too late.

00:08:29.426 --> 00:08:30.552
What floor?

00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:33.305
Let's try the fourth floor like usual.

00:08:33.305 --> 00:08:35.474
Okay.

00:08:35.474 --> 00:08:38.727
Barbeque, barbeque!

00:08:44.858 --> 00:08:47.402
Sorry I'm late.

00:08:47.402 --> 00:08:49.571
Something wrong?

00:08:49.571 --> 00:08:52.157
Actually, we're going to...

00:08:52.157 --> 00:08:53.367
Huh?

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.371
What? What?!

00:08:57.371 --> 00:09:01.834
Let me off of this thing!

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:05.045
--No, no, no, no, no.

00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:05.587
--It won't take long. Hang in there.
--No, no, no, no, no.

00:09:05.587 --> 00:09:08.048
--It won't take long. Hang in there.
--I can't. I can't. I can't. I can't. I can't.

00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:08.632
--All we have to do is
find Akari and bring her back.
--I can't. I can't. I can't. I can't. I can't.

00:09:08.632 --> 00:09:11.385
--All we have to do is
find Akari and bring her back.
--Lemme off. Lemme off. Lemme off. Lemme off.

00:09:11.385 --> 00:09:12.511
--Lemme off. Lemme off. Lemme off. Lemme off.

00:09:12.511 --> 00:09:15.138
You'll be in more danger if you get off now.

00:09:15.138 --> 00:09:16.723
What do you mean?

00:09:16.723 --> 00:09:20.435
We don't know where the In-Between begins.

00:09:32.781 --> 00:09:34.408
What the hell are those for?

00:09:34.408 --> 00:09:35.826
The fifth floor is a little...

00:09:35.826 --> 00:09:36.702
A little what?

00:09:36.702 --> 00:09:38.620
There's a weird girl there.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.455
What do you mean, a weird girl?

00:09:40.455 --> 00:09:43.876
On the fifth floor, there's this girl
who always tries to get in.

00:09:43.876 --> 00:09:47.171
But that's in Jinbo-cho.
I don't know if she'll be here, too.

00:09:47.171 --> 00:09:49.673
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:09:49.673 --> 00:09:52.050
A girl who always tries
to get in on the fifth floor?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.886
That's totally terrifying!

00:09:53.886 --> 00:09:55.637
Almost there.

00:09:59.933 --> 00:10:01.351
Huh?

00:10:07.566 --> 00:10:10.194
Akari?

00:10:10.194 --> 00:10:12.070
Akari!

00:10:15.157 --> 00:10:17.868
What now?

00:10:17.868 --> 00:10:22.789
What happens if you get off the
elevator on the way to the Otherside?

00:10:22.789 --> 00:10:25.209
Who knows? I definitely don't.

00:10:25.209 --> 00:10:28.629
The urban legend doesn't say.

00:10:28.629 --> 00:10:31.340
But...

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.509
We have to find her.

00:10:33.509 --> 00:10:34.927
Right.

00:10:34.927 --> 00:10:39.056
Hey, wait, you guys! Jeez!

00:10:50.359 --> 00:10:53.111
This is really weird.

00:10:53.111 --> 00:10:56.073
This building definitely wasn't this big.

00:10:56.073 --> 00:11:01.245
I've no idea what the
In-Between is supposed to be like.

00:11:01.245 --> 00:11:04.706
In some ways, it may be even
stranger than the Otherside.

00:11:04.706 --> 00:11:10.003
Yeah, that cat town was pretty strange, too.

00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:14.132
It was strange but in a cute way.

00:11:14.132 --> 00:11:18.846
I would've explored it a bit more
if we hadn't been attacked by ninja cats.

00:11:18.846 --> 00:11:20.848
Hey.

00:11:20.848 --> 00:11:25.185
I don't know how you two
can act like this is no big deal.

00:11:25.185 --> 00:11:27.855
Don't worry. We're on high alert.

00:11:27.855 --> 00:11:32.025
That's not what I meant.
I don't get how you're not freaked out.

00:11:32.025 --> 00:11:35.362
We're scared, but there's
no point talking about it.

00:11:35.362 --> 00:11:37.906
Is it too much for you? Want a piggyback ride?

00:11:37.906 --> 00:11:40.951
Huh? Don't make fun of me!

00:11:40.951 --> 00:11:42.578
It was just a suggestion.

00:11:42.578 --> 00:11:46.290
Damn it, I know that.
Just lead the way, already.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:49.751
Let's hurry. We gotta catch up to Akari, quick.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:55.382
Jeez, it's like this every time with you guys.

00:11:55.382 --> 00:11:59.511
There's someone way closer to you
than Akari, and she's totally terrified.

00:11:59.511 --> 00:12:02.973
So how about showing some concern for me, too?

00:12:02.973 --> 00:12:06.268
But you're not the one in danger right now.

00:12:06.268 --> 00:12:09.563
Just my luck!

00:12:09.563 --> 00:12:14.443
Why am I a magnet for women
who don't care about others?

00:12:14.443 --> 00:12:17.196
What was that? It didn't very sound very nice.

00:12:17.196 --> 00:12:22.075
I just said you're the kind of woman
who doesn't care about others.

00:12:22.075 --> 00:12:24.077
Then what do you suggest we do?

00:12:24.077 --> 00:12:28.749
We can't abandon Akari,
and we can't leave you here.

00:12:28.749 --> 00:12:31.126
So that's what's going through your head.

00:12:31.126 --> 00:12:33.879
So then, what? We should abandon her?

00:12:33.879 --> 00:12:40.719
No. I was just shocked that you
actually wanted to help someone.

00:12:40.719 --> 00:12:42.763
What kind of a person do you think I am?

00:12:42.763 --> 00:12:43.805
--The kind that doesn't care--

00:12:43.805 --> 00:12:44.556
--Hey, cut it out.
--The kind that doesn't care--

00:12:44.556 --> 00:12:45.557
--Hey, cut it out.

00:12:45.557 --> 00:12:47.226
Look.

00:12:57.903 --> 00:12:59.738
Akari?

00:13:28.475 --> 00:13:32.437
H-Hey, what are you doing? Don't!

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:02.509
Sorawo, that way.

00:14:02.509 --> 00:14:04.261
Let's go.

00:14:04.261 --> 00:14:07.097
I don't know if I can do this.

00:14:57.606 --> 00:14:59.483
Akari!

00:14:59.483 --> 00:15:02.236
Akari!

00:15:02.236 --> 00:15:04.363
Akari!

00:15:07.699 --> 00:15:09.201
Can't you hear me?

00:15:09.201 --> 00:15:12.162
Huh? Sorawo? Hi.

00:15:12.162 --> 00:15:14.456
But why are you behind me?

00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:19.253
Didn't you hear me? I kept calling your name.

00:15:19.253 --> 00:15:23.173
What? You were up ahead of me
the whole time, weren't you?

00:15:23.173 --> 00:15:23.757
--What?

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:24.925
--You got it backwards.
We were chasing after you.
--What?

00:15:24.925 --> 00:15:27.469
--You got it backwards.
We were chasing after you.

00:15:27.469 --> 00:15:31.181
But I saw someone with long hair.
I thought it was you, Sorawo.

00:15:31.181 --> 00:15:34.059
I've been chasing <i>you </i>the whole time.

00:15:37.396 --> 00:15:42.234
But my hair's not actually that long.

00:15:42.234 --> 00:15:44.820
Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:49.908
Why'd I think it was you?

00:15:56.957 --> 00:16:00.127
What the hell's that?
It's coming this way. What is it?

00:16:00.127 --> 00:16:02.629
Stand back, Kozakura.

00:16:02.629 --> 00:16:04.423
Sorawo?

00:16:09.803 --> 00:16:12.264
Sorawo, what is it?

00:16:17.269 --> 00:16:20.189
Toriko, your hand is...

00:16:21.398 --> 00:16:23.692
It feels all tingly.

00:16:23.692 --> 00:16:26.737
This one's really dangerous.

00:16:27.779 --> 00:16:30.365
Quick, run!

00:16:32.618 --> 00:16:36.538
That's so weird. I thought that was you, Sorawo.

00:16:36.538 --> 00:16:38.457
How could you possibly think that?

00:16:38.457 --> 00:16:42.586
Can't I shoot it like usual?
You know, while you're watching it?

00:16:42.586 --> 00:16:47.090
I can take it on, too.
If you watch me, I could...

00:16:49.343 --> 00:16:51.929
Looks like it's growing.

00:16:53.722 --> 00:16:57.226
Guns and karate aren't gonna work on this one.

00:16:57.226 --> 00:16:58.477
We gotta run!

00:16:58.477 --> 00:17:00.354
Run? Where?

00:17:00.354 --> 00:17:02.606
The elevator! Let's get back there!

00:17:02.606 --> 00:17:06.235
We gotta go through that
pain-in-the-ass procedure again?

00:17:06.235 --> 00:17:08.820
We only have to press the
first floor to get back... probably!

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:11.156
Did you just say probably?!

00:17:17.162 --> 00:17:18.789
This is why I didn't wanna come!

00:17:18.789 --> 00:17:21.458
God damn it! You're gonna pay for this.

00:17:21.458 --> 00:17:22.584
Shit!

00:17:22.584 --> 00:17:23.544
Kozakura!

00:17:23.544 --> 00:17:25.128
Don't be stupid! Keep running!

00:17:25.128 --> 00:17:27.464
Forget about me! Run!

00:17:27.464 --> 00:17:28.298
But...

00:17:28.298 --> 00:17:32.594
Keep running! And don't wait
if the elevator's ready to go!

00:17:34.429 --> 00:17:35.931
I thought you were scared.

00:17:35.931 --> 00:17:39.101
Of course, I'm scared, you moron!
I'm gonna kill you!

00:17:39.101 --> 00:17:41.728
Huh? B-But...

00:17:43.355 --> 00:17:45.315
There it is!

00:19:10.025 --> 00:19:13.695
Satsuki... Uruma.

00:19:48.272 --> 00:19:49.439
Are we back?

00:19:49.439 --> 00:19:51.984
I-I don't know.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:59.241
"Gyurakutei Charcoal-Grilled Japanese BBQ"

00:20:07.833 --> 00:20:10.752
We made it back.

00:20:10.752 --> 00:20:12.129
That was close.

00:20:12.129 --> 00:20:15.799
That was seriously not cool.
I never wanna do that again.

00:20:15.799 --> 00:20:19.011
Going out for barbeque
is way harder than I thought.

00:20:22.347 --> 00:20:24.474
I'm hungry.

00:20:24.474 --> 00:20:26.393
We did get quite a workout.

00:20:26.393 --> 00:20:29.438
Seriously? I totally lost my appetite.

00:20:29.438 --> 00:20:33.400
I'm never going out to eat
with you people again.

00:20:36.445 --> 00:20:40.699
Oh, thanks. But why does my hand feel all weird?

00:20:40.699 --> 00:20:43.410
Sorry. I used it to get us back.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.537
Oh, okay. I don't mind.

00:20:45.537 --> 00:20:46.955
Sorawo!

00:20:46.955 --> 00:20:50.334
What was that? What just happened?

00:20:50.334 --> 00:20:52.628
Don't ask me. I have no idea.

00:20:52.628 --> 00:20:54.838
Really?

00:20:54.838 --> 00:20:58.300
Excuse me. We have a reservation.
Kamikoshi, party of four.

00:20:58.300 --> 00:21:02.429
She made a reservation? Why'd she use my name?

00:21:02.429 --> 00:21:04.556
Because she knew you'd come?

00:21:04.556 --> 00:21:06.433
Well, I did come...

00:21:06.433 --> 00:21:10.312
And I went to save Akari, too.

00:21:10.312 --> 00:21:13.190
Now no one can say I don't care about others.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:14.191
Totally!

00:21:14.191 --> 00:21:15.108
I know, right?

00:21:15.108 --> 00:21:18.695
Then again, it was the obvious thing to do.

00:21:18.695 --> 00:21:21.114
Your standard for "obvious" is too high.

00:21:21.114 --> 00:21:22.115
Is it?

00:21:22.115 --> 00:21:26.912
Yeah! That was terrifying,
but I went to save her anyway.

00:21:26.912 --> 00:21:29.456
I don't think just anyone could do that.

00:21:29.456 --> 00:21:32.501
Hmm, I wonder...

00:21:32.501 --> 00:21:37.005
When you put it that way,
Kozakura might be the most caring of all.

00:21:37.005 --> 00:21:37.840
Huh?

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:39.883
Okay, let's eat some Japanese barbeque!

00:21:39.883 --> 00:21:42.678
Hey, get the lead out. C'mon!

00:21:42.678 --> 00:21:44.555
Your treat, right?

00:21:44.555 --> 00:21:45.806
You bet!

00:21:45.806 --> 00:21:47.474
Let's go.

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:52.563
This really sucks.

00:21:53.605 --> 00:21:57.568
"How to Get to the
Barbeque Restaurant by Elevator"

00:22:11.623 --> 00:22:15.878
<i>My hair was tossed by the cold wind</i>

00:22:15.878 --> 00:22:20.007
<i>Did you notice me shut the window?</i>

00:22:20.007 --> 00:22:24.303
<i>I lose my nerve when we get so close</i>

00:22:24.303 --> 00:22:28.182
<i>I don't need something that won't last</i>

00:22:28.182 --> 00:22:30.309
<i>Flashbacks hurt</i>

00:22:30.309 --> 00:22:31.935
<i>Ever-lingering shadows</i>

00:22:31.935 --> 00:22:36.106
<i>I know I'm too bound by the past, aren't I?</i>

00:22:36.106 --> 00:22:38.525
<i>Hey, this feeling we felt</i>

00:22:38.525 --> 00:22:44.114
<i>There's no doubt about it,</i>
<i>it's got to be special</i>

00:22:44.114 --> 00:22:47.951
<i>You and me, crisscrossing emotions</i>

00:22:47.951 --> 00:22:52.164
<i>I don't want to look back with regret</i>

00:22:52.164 --> 00:22:57.002
<i>I tell myself to believe</i>

00:22:57.002 --> 00:23:00.964
<i>And I tell my heart,</i>
<i>trust me, trust me, so sparkly</i>

00:23:00.964 --> 00:23:04.760
<i>It's the rhythm of a racing pulse</i>

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:08.972
<i>As I gazed at your outstretched hand</i>

00:23:08.972 --> 00:23:15.103
<i>I decided I'd put my trust in you</i>

00:23:15.103 --> 00:23:23.529
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>

00:23:23.529 --> 00:23:30.911
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will</i>

00:23:32.621 --> 00:23:34.581
Did you stop growing your hair out?

00:23:34.581 --> 00:23:39.086
Hm? Oh, yeah. I decided my
usual length works just fine.

00:23:39.086 --> 00:23:41.129
But I appreciated the compliment.

00:23:41.129 --> 00:23:43.799
Oh, okay. Short is nice, too.

00:23:43.799 --> 00:23:47.094
I wish she'd make up her mind!
